                                 CHAPTER 2

    THE WISDOM OF FOCUSED VISION

Vision is the ideation in your mind of a desired future reality. It is a
prerequisite for success in life. When there is no vision, life becomes a
guess work and leads nowhere. Prov. 29:18 says, ‘when there is no vision,
people cast off restraint…’ Thus, whenever you see someone living an
‘anything-goes’ kind of life, you just met someone with no life vision.
Visionary people know where they are going and constrain their lives
only to activities and engagements that take them there.

It is important to note that vision is beyond having an ambition to
become something. Having life ambitions has been popularised among
young people especially in our schools, but it is important to teach
Kingdom citizens that life vision is not just the career one desires to
succeed at. It is the assignment God has given you for your life. There is
no harm in people of the world developing a life ambition and pursuing
it, but for a child of God, genuine one’s life vision should be God-
inspired. This is because success in the Kingdom is not merely measured
by material accomplishment, but by fulfilling one’s God-given
assignment. Your vision is a mind-picture of your life purpose.
Knowing and pursuing God’s vision for your life is a foundational
wisdom for living.

Focusing on your life vision is a master secret to greatness in life. Have
you ever been to an artist’s studio and observed the level of focus with
which he creates his masterpiece? Why does a carpenter focus with
precision as he hits nails held between his fingers?

                                                               6
                                    THE WISDOM OF FOCUSED VISION

Why this level of care? Because the slightest misuse of the hammer can
cost him his fingers. So, for the carpenter to achieve his carpentry goals
and also to avoid injuries on his finger, he will engage the wisdom of
focus. Focus has been defined by someone as ‘Following on Course
Until Success’.

Having understood clearly what your life assignment and vision is, you
need to focus on fulfilling it. Focus starts by preparing yourself for the
future you have seen in your mind. Note that during the time of
preparation for your vision, there are lots of distractions. For example,
someone may have a vision of becoming a great musician and is a
soccer lover. While both music and soccer are harmless past times, such
person needs to know which one is the vision and which is the
distraction. Thus, he may need to regulate the time spent on soccer and
pour more time into musical rehearsals, if he is serious about becoming
a “world class musician”. There is also a need for focus when one has
fully stepped into one’s vision. At this point, there are lots of
compromises calling for attention; focus is keeping the main thing as the
main thing. It is wise to minimise goals per time. Do not just have a
long list of goals that spread your life thin, rather prioritise and pursue
your goals in order of importance and impact on your vision. This will
prevent you from dissipating your energy haphazardly and help you to
get desired results in life.

The Bible instructs in Prov. 4:25 (Amp) "Let your eyes look right on
[with fixed purpose], and let your gaze be straight before you”. What are
you aiming to shoot? Even if you have the best of all bows and the finest
of all arrows; and you are the most skilled of all archers; you need
focus! You only shoot well when you focus well on your target. An
unfocused shot will only make one expend energy unto futility, resulting
in an unprofitable use of time. Focused vision will help you make the
best use of your time, and productive use of your energy.

                                                               7
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

A resolution you should make every day of your life is to remain firm,
unbending and dogged as you go about actualizing your vision.

