                                 CHAPTER 4

           THE WISDOM OF AUTOMATION

Greatness is a cumulus of simple but consistent routines that develop
over time. The most valid factor to vet greatness is to check the track
record of the routines that led to it. Automated routine is the genius of
greatness. Wise and exceptional people have learnt the secret of
automating the routines that account for their success in life.

Most people do great things here and there. Nearly everybody works
out once in a while, reads a good book, takes a daring step to move
forward when they are pressured by life, or creatively solves problems as
the occasion presents. However, the difference between exceptional
people and average people is that great people consistently do the great
things that average people do once in a while.

To think about it, most students, including those with low academic
grade points, have gotten a good grade in at least a course at some
point. However, the first-class student does not get distinction once in a
while; he/she gets an ‘A’ grade as a routine. If you want to know how
great your life will be, check your routines. If you want to be successful
and great, automate the routines that make for greatness in life.
Automating your daily life for success is great wisdom.

When God created the heavens and the earth, he ordered and
automated the daily running of the universe. According to Gen 1: 14,

                                                              12
                                       THE WISDOM OF AUTOMATION

Then God said, ‘‘Let there be lights in the firmament of the heavens to
divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs and seasons, and
for days and years.’

God has never needed to create another daybreak since the first; He
does not command the day to break every morning and set every
evening. From creation, He automated the dawn of the day and the
dusk of the night. These routines automatically run by God’s initial
command. Psalm 148: 5 says, God established them forever and forever.
His orders will never be revoked. Have you ordered your yearly,
monthly, weekly or daily routine in such a way that it runs
automatically to deliver all round success?

The signature of the wisdom of automation is seen everywhere in
nature. Since God created the first fruit and herb, He has never had to
revisit to create another. He automated a system for reproduction in all
living things. Thus Genesis 8:22 says, "While the earth remaineth,
seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day
and night shall not cease."

The Law of Automation is the master key to consistency and
commitment. When there is an automated routine that you live up to,
your life performance is not left to mood or chance. Many people are
largely regulated by emotions which vacillate irregularly. So, a person
makes a decision for greatness and draws out goals and disciplines he
needs to pursue and get fulfilled. But, at the very next moment, he has
wandered off the goal and suddenly becomes so indifferent to the
pursuit of the goals he had set. Why? It is because he is being regulated
by situations, emotions and emergencies of life. It is wise for your life to
be regulated by routines and systems.

The following are some things to automate into your life for success:

                                                              13
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

1. Have a daily prayer time : You can achieve this either by having
prayer times or periods. You can also have a community or
accountability group that you join to pray at particular times.

2. Have a study program: have books that you are reading weekly or
monthly and even courses you take monthly or quarterly - write all
these out from the beginning of the year.

3. Automate impact by having a platform that runs periodically and
perpetually where you dispense value either for profit or non-profit.

4. Automate financial savings and investment by having a percentage of
your income set aside for your future.

5. Automate money making habits: Either by writing on a blog, selling
products, curating promo packages that you can run at special periods
etc.

6. Automate your waking up time and morning rituals: exercises,
meditation, prayers, listening to motivation or sermons etc.

7. Automate rest: siesta, vacation or retreat time daily, weekly, monthly
or yearly as applicable.

8. Automate time spent with loved ones either daily, weekly or monthly
dates, picnics, family time at meals etc.

                                                              14
