                                 CHAPTER 5

               THE WISDOM OF ORDER

Order is doing the right thing at the right time in the right place. Order
is the harbinger of excellence. In fact, excellence has been defined as
attaining the highest level of order in a particular venture. Order is
paying attention to details and making sure everything is as it ought to
be. An orderly life is the requirement for growth, greatness and
productivity. Anything that is out of order saps energy and waste effort.
You must make sure you live an ordered life.

God is obsessed with order and proper arrangement. When we study
how God paid attention to details at creation, we’ll know that he is a
God of order. The orderliness of the skies, the stars, the seasons, the
water-cycle, carbon-cycle, and nature shows that God is a stickler for
order. Wherever we see disorder in nature, man has interfered. Order is
when all parts of something whole stay where they should and work
together harmoniously for a desirable outcome. Order is a signature of
God.

1 Cor. 14:40 says let all things be done decently and in order. No one
should act disorderly in the name of being spiritual. Even in Church
meetings, there is what is called the order of service. Meaning even the
service, ruled and directed by the Holy Spirit should have an order.
Many Christians do not plan or put order in place and hide under the
pretext that they will do ‘as the Spirit leads’.

                                                              16
                                             THE WIDOM OF ORDER

While it is true that the Holy Spirit might break or disrupt human order
when He starts moving, He is not an enemy of order. The Holy Spirit
loves order and many times, might even demand for order to be in place
before He blesses or moves upon something.

The book of Numbers is an Old Testament classic on order. God
ordered the position where everything was to be put. He specified the
dressing for every priest and for every person that was to carry out a
task for Him. He was clear on who was in charge of every assignment
and gadget in the Tabernacle and in the entire nation of Israel. He gave
details on where each tribe was to camp and who was to move first
when they were to start a journey and those to stop first when it was
time to rest. God left nothing to chance, He gave sitting arrangement,
dressing arrangement, movement instructions, allocated tasks,
responsibility and position and insisted that everyone do what they are
supposed to do without breaking order. God is obsessed with order.
Living an orderly life is Godlikeness.

Another striking order in the Book of Number is the orderly
documentation of every fact. The details with which the statistics of the
civilization which lived thousands of year were recorded and kept till
date shows that order is a divine wisdom that only God gives and is not
necessarily acquired through school education. Many educated
individuals and organisations do not have the level of facts, figures and
statistics that the primitive nation of Israel provided and preserved till
date about all the records and details of their nation and journey. Truly,
order is a God-given wisdom and is not merely human taught. This is
why it is right to pray for the wisdom to be orderly in all areas of life.

In African parlance, a disorderly life is called an “anyhow life’ or
‘anything goes’ lifestyle. Disorderly people are always threatened by
order and they fight it.

                                                              17
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

Order or disorder shows in a person’s gait, grooming, dressing, speech,
driving and working. When order is put in place and a particular person
or people complain and love to violate order in that environment, you
have met a person who is naturally disorderly and wants the
environment to take their own shape. It is lack of a structure of order
around one’s life that gets many people into the troubles they get into.
Disorder is the reason anybody enters into your private space anyhow.
Some people are so disorderly that nearly all friends and acquaintances
have access to their bedroom - worst still, their unkempt bedroom. Part
of order is demarcating and drawing lines around your life to know who
belongs where and who cannot have access to certain things and places
in your life and space. Whether kept or unkempt, there are spaces in
your life and environment that should be demarcated as non-public.

Another area of order is time management. It is disorder that makes a
person, a meeting or an organization always run late. Let’s be orderly in
managing time and doing what is only proper for the time. It is
disorderly to receive a person who did not book an appointment and
gist for hours because he/she said they was passing by and thought to
say ‘hi’ to you. Order shows in the arrangement of our environment.
One way to know an orderly people is to examine their homes ,offices
and private spaces.

1 Tim 3:2 says, for a pastor must be a good man whose life cannot be
spoken against. He must have only one wife, and he must be hard working
and thoughtful, ORDERLY, and full of good deeds. . . (TLB)
A leader must be orderly in conduct and behaviour. An unruly conduct
and conversation is the foolishness of disorder. Behave orderly and
speak like a gentleman and lady with sound etiquette. Another area
where order cannot be overlooked is in dressing. Going through the
Bible, we see that God is specific about dressing for His people.
Indecent and immoral dressing is wrong by all ramifications and is
disorderly for a leader, most especially a Christian.

                                                              18
                                            THE WISDOM OF ORDER

Nudity is not a virtue, neither is dressing unruly. Have you ever
watched the United Nations proceedings and seen presidents in torn-
jeans, with low hanging belts, tattoos and diamond chains around their
necks? What about secretaries of state wearing revealing spaghetti wears
with low hanging-cleavage-reveal-sleeveless shirts on butt-tight
miniskirts? Some things are not issues of religious talks but honour,
order and etiquette. Also, stone-age dressing, tattered, pauperised
dressing, uncultured dressing and unfashionable dressing are neither
glorifying. Excellent dressing is part of order, let’s be orderly.

The level of order in your personal life dictates the order in your
organization and work. Do you know that order that you develop in
your personal hygiene and grooming, home and office arrangement,
and general daily life will spill over to your work, career, enterprise and
business. Every organization and platform generally assumes the level
of order demonstrated by its members, especially the leader(s).

A strong determinant of organizational order is the flow of authority
within the organization. There cannot be order within a people and an
organization until there is clear cut definition of who is answerable to
who, who has authority to dictate to who and who must honour and
submit to who. There must also be clear-cut and non-clashing job
descriptions for every person in the organization. The truth is that an
organization – nation, business, ministry, government or non-
governmental cannot grow beyond the level of order it puts in place.
One of the highest duties of leadership is to put and maintain order.

Order is important in our personal lives and in the way we do things.
Proper order in doing things talks about the do and don’ts in
methodologies of things. Do not just put good order in place in your
personal life, let everything you do be according to due order.

                                                              19
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

There is proper order in communication lines in an organization. There
is due order in business communication and it is different from informal
conversation. There is a right order in relating with the opposite gender,
There is also due order in ministry as regards relating with the people
and resources God commits in your hands. Whenever people violate
order, they incur grave consequences. 1 Chron. 15:13 says, For because
you did not do it the first time, the Lord our God broke out against us,
because we did not consult Him about the proper order (NKJV). In this
scripture, they were doing a good thing but someone lost his life because
he violated the order of how it ought to be done. It is not enough to
know what to do, you must find out how to do it and the proper order
that governs doing it. You can never get favour and approval in a place
or with a person that you violate the laid down order. Following laid
down order is one of the fastest ways to secure favour with a person or
group.

