candlestick, that they which enter in may see the light. For nothing is
secret, that shall not be made manifest; neither any thing hid, that shall
not be known and come abroad’. If man will not keep forever in secret a
candle they light, how much more will God put on an exalted place a
person He has lighted in the place of solitude.

Ultimately, Jesus Christ was a master practitioner of the wisdom of
solitude.
The next mention about Jesus after the stories surrounding His birth
was when He was twelve years. Thereafter, He was in oblivion till he
was thirty years. This season was definitely not idled away; it was spent
in diligent preparation. When Jesus showed up on the scene at the age
of thirty, He was baptised and the Holy Spirit came upon Him.
Immediately, after being filled with the Holy Spirit, he was again led by
the Spirit into the wilderness where he was alone in the wilderness for 40
days and nights and there had encounters that chartered His destiny
and ministry. The concept of being alone to have life and destiny
encounters is an indisputable trend in the scripture.

                                                              25
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

After Jesus returned from the place of solitude in the wilderness,
scripture says that “Then Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit to
Galilee…” (Luke 4:14)
Everyone who aspires to be great must learn the act of withdrawing into
solitude. Great people chase the secret place and not the stage because
in the kingdom. The place of solitude is also the secret place. The secret
place is where God meets with man individually and privately, that is to
say that the secret place is not in the church or at a prayer meeting even
though God is in those gatherings too.

Jesus set the precedence of valuing the secret place for all believers.
Thus, after He started ministry, he periodically withdrew into the secret
place until the final moments in Gethsemane where He was alone with
God to prepare for the cross (Matt 26: 36 - 38). In fact, Jesus counted
periodic withdrawal into solitude so important that he had to school
His disciples in the Art and Wisdom of Solitude. In Luke 9:10-11, Then
the apostles returned, they reported to Jesus what they had done. Then he
took them with him and they withdrew by themselves to a town called
Bethsaida, but the crowds learned about it and followed him. Luke 5:16
says, But Jesus often withdrew to the wilderness for prayer. Also in John
6:15-16, Jesus, knowing that they intended to come and make him king by
force, withdrew again to a mountain by himself.
Jesus constantly practised the Wisdom of Solitude and so should you.

                                                              26
                                 CHAPTER 7

             THE WISDOM OF BUILDING

Wisdom is required in building anything commendable. Prov. 24: 3
says, through skillful and godly wisdom is a house (a life, a home, a
family, an enterprise, a business, a ministry, an organisation) built, and by
understanding it is established (on a sound and good foundation).
(AMP Version, some additions, mine). Anywhere you see anything well
built, wisdom was employed. Wisdom is justified by what it builds. If
you want to build anything that men will see and commend, you must
be intentional about using wisdom. .
In 1 Cor. 3: 10, Paul says, by the grace given to me, I laid a foundation as
a wise builder, and someone else is building on it. But each one should
build with care. The level of wisdom of a person can be determined by
the quality of what he has built or is building with his or her life. Do not
just live from day to day, let the daily activities of your life be
cumulative in building something specific. Whatever you are building
must be related to your goals. Your activities, time, resources
investment and spiritual/mental exertion must revolve round what you
are building. You must go through life with the mindset of a builder.

The following are things to build with your lifetime:
1. Build a relationship with God: Good relationships do not just happen,
they are deliberately built. Time is a major ingredient for building a
relationship. Another key component in building a good relationship is
prioritisation.

                                                              27
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

 Many legitimate things will compete for your time and attention, but,
for you to build a relationship with God, you have to deliberately plan
and prioritize times of prayer, meditation, study of God’s word,
fellowshipping with other believers, serving and impacting people for
God. It is wisdom to always create time for God no matter how busy
you get.

2. Build people: A life lived for one’s self alone is an unfulfilled one. You
must have a set of people you are building and raising. The people you
build today will be your reward tomorrow. Opportunity to build people
abounds in every area of life and irrespective of location. There are both
online and onsite platforms for impacting people. Do not just live a life
of surviving day to day and earning to make a living, have people you
are building and be intentional about it.

3. Build a Financial System: An employee cannot transfer their
employed job to their progeny but they can transfer ownership of
business they built. This shows us that it is only what you build that you
ever really own. It is great wisdom to build a business. While it is not
everyone that might have the skill and training to succeed as an
entrepreneur, some will succeed as intrapreneurs. However it is most
important that everyone owns a financial system that you can pass over
as a legacy. This could be a business, an investment or an income
generating asset. Prov. 27: 24 says develop your business first before
building your house (NLT).

4. Build a family: Family is God’s provision for giving and receiving
love. Even the All-Wise God built a big universal family where He is
‘Father’. Family brings accountability, responsibility and sanity to a
life. It is a wise thing to build a family.

                                                              28
                                          THE WISDOM OF BUILDING

5. Build a Good Name: Build a reputation for yourself. Prov. 22: 2 says a
good name is rather to be chosen than great riches and loving favour
rather than silver and gold. It is important to build a name that will be
an asset to open doors for people. Let the mention of your name be an
access key to people. You must also be deliberate on putting a name
and a brand on things you do. Many people do fantastic things but
without the consciousness of building a name. Have a name for that
venture, meeting or platform where you dispense value to a few people.
Things grow better when they have a name. Many times, the greatness
you seek is in the greatness of the name of that thing you are building.
So God told Abraham, “I will make you a great nation, I will bless you
and make your name great”. Enoch Adeboye existed as an unknown
name until Christ the Redeemer’s Ministries/Redeemed Christian
Church of God was built to become a great ministry. Bill Gates became
a great name because Microsoft became a great company. Whether in
the spiritual or corporate realms, the law is the same; your greatness is
linked to the greatness of the name or brand you are building. Note that
you may be either the pioneer or the associate in the name you are
building, it does not really matter. David Abioye is a great name
because Living Faith was built to greatness even though he is not the
president of the organisation. If you are not a pioneer, it is strategic to
consider the greatness and goodwill or the potentials of a name in
deciding where to affiliate yourself.

6. Build a House: it is a blessing to own your home. Do not be
comfortable as a tenant, no matter how nice your landlord or house-
agent is. The amount some people spend on a rented apartment and
luxury is alarming when they do not have a land or home to their own
name anywhere. Build houses to rent to others and own your own
home. The earlier you build a house, the better.

                                                              29
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

We must believe God for a new flow of God’s blessing where the
majority of His children own their own houses as young people even
before marriage.

7. Build a Platform: There should be a platform where you dispense
value to the world. A platform is a meeting point between you and
people for the purpose of exchange of value. Do not just work for the
sake of earning a livelihood all through life. Make sure you build a
platform for dispensing your inherent values to people. Most times,
your platform is the stream and the determinant of your rewards in life.
It could be physical or virtual, but make sure there is a platform that
you have built to deliver and dispense your inherent giftings to the
world. A platform could be a ministry, business, charity organisation,
etc. It is very good and profitable to join an existing platform. However,
it is also powerful to create your own platform, even if it is as a subset
or as a complementary set to the platform you joined. In other words, it
is okay to join an existing system, but the platform must afford you the
opportunity to dispense your individual contribution in a way that you
are also positioned for reward. In some cases, it is possible and wise to
create a platform that runs uniquely, uncompetitively and
simultaneously with the platform you are part of.

8. Build wealth: There is a difference between making money and
building wealth. To build wealth, you must carefully amalgamate a
portfolio of multiple streams of income for consistent inflow and
growth of wealth. Wealth building demands that there are financial
streams that bring consistent cash flow to you so that you are never
short of money to meet your immediate expenditure. At the same time
they are streams that are able to do capital projects so that you can
advance financially through targeted gains.

                                                              30
                                          THE WISDOM OF BUILDING

Different streams of income includes: wages from job/work, profits
from business/sales, dividends from investments and paper, royalties
and honorariums from impact or one-time products, rentals from
assets/real estates, etc. Creating wealth is strategically diversifying your i
streams of income and investments so that your finances grow
sustainably and consistently. According to Prov. 13:22 , a good man
leaves an inheritance to his children’s children.

9. Build a legacy: Building a legacy is very vital in life. What will you
bequeath to the generation coming after you? Leaving a legacy is not
just leaving behind money or assets for your children. Building a legacy
is building all of the above named points such that when you retire from
active service or leave the earth, there is something tangible that your
life has produced and future generations received as a proof of your life
well lived.

