Ownership is a blessing: even though there are things that are
economically cheaper when leased than owned. However, many times,
the issue of ownership goes beyond mere financial bottom-line. It goes
into the spirit of our spiritual right as children of God. Thus, when it
comes to dealing with things that are cheaper to lease than to own; it is
still better to own those things and make money from leasing out some
parts of its use to offset the additional cost of ownership. For instance,
someone may argue that it makes more economic sense for him/her to
use public transport than to own a car. While that may be very true, the
blessing of ownership is beyond financial calculations, it goes into the
spirit of freedom, liberty and spiritual blessing. Therefore, it is
financially smart to own a car and then factor out a way to make money
from it through commercialising some parts of one’s use of the car so
that the additional income can offset some parts of the cost of
ownership. Ownership is ultimately always wise than renting.

