surrounding borders, were deeded to Abraham. It is important to know
that someone lending you their possession to use for free is still not
ownership. While that is a form of favour, the real favour is the one that
brings you into ownership.

This is also seen in 2 Samuel 24 when David wanted to make a sacrifice
to God on the land of Araunah who volunteered to give it to him for
use. David insisted on buying it. In 2 Samuel 24:24, then the king said to
Araunah, “No, but I will surely buy it from you for a price; nor will I offer
burnt offerings to the Lord my God with that which costs me nothing.” So
David bought the threshing floor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver.
2 Samuel 24:25 And David built there an altar to the Lord, and offered
burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the Lord heeded the prayers for
the land, and the plague was withdrawn from Israel. It was on this land
bought by David that Solomon later build the Lord’s Temple years later

                                                              37
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

and a generational stream of blessing was sealed for his lineage. This is
shown in 2 Chron. 3:1-2, Now Solomon began to build the house of the
Lord at Jerusalem on Mount Moriah, where the Lord had appeared to his
father David, at the place that David had prepared on the threshing floor
of Ornan (variant of Araunah) the Jebusite. And he began to build on the
second day of the second month in the fourth year of his reign.

Imagine the spiritual blessing that comes from being the owner of the
land where God’s House is built and nations come to worship God. All
that blessing would have gone to Araunah’s lineage if David took the
land for free use and did not purchase it for ownership. I have seen
people buy lands and telecommunication multinationals later come to
lease it for a mast paying periodic huge dividends. If that land was
borrowed or leased, that blessing would go to the owner not to the user.
Ownership of land is setting up your children for a huge blessing.

Ownership is dominion; we have dominion over what we own. But what
we must not allow what we own, to have dominion over us. In other
words, you are to own things and they are not to own you. God is
actually the only real owner and we are stewards of whatever He allows
us to own - this is stewardship in ownership. We must pursue ownership
with the mindset of stewardship. The acid test of stewardship is that
whatever you own, you are willing and able to lay down when God
demands for it. The consciousness a believer in ownership should live
with is that "I am actually not the real owner of all I own; I'm just being
privileged to be a steward managing God's resources in my hands." For
believers with such heart, there is no limit to what God can commit into
their hands. Thus, the wisdom of ownership is not merely an obsession
to accumulate possessions, but a desire for advancement of God’s
kingdom through our control of earthly resources for Him.

                                                              38
                                        THE WISDOM OF OWNERSHIP

Like Abraham in Gen 22: 1- 18, who laid down Isaac, there is nothing
God commits into our hands that we should not be able to lay down.
The wisdom of ownership must be accompanied with the wisdom of
stewardship.

