                                 CHAPTER 9

        THE WISDOM OF INDEPENDENCE

All humans were born dependent - starting from the period of gestation
when the human fetus was entirely dependent on their mother for food,
water, air and every other thing needed for life, to when the baby is
born and it becomes utterly dependent on people around. This is a
deliberate design from God to humble everyone so that there is no one
that can lay claim to utter independence throughout their lifetime. The
very place of utter independence on any other is reserved by Elohim for
Himself. ‘Elohim’ means ‘The Self-Existent, Self-Sustaining, Eternal
One’.

Thus, it is okay to be dependent on others at certain points in life. As a
matter of fact, throughout our lifetime, we will always have reasons to
be dependent on others for one thing or the other. Therefore, ‘The
Wisdom of Dependence’ is something every one that will succeed in life
must have. We must know when we need others and must be humble
enough to receive their help and input. Additionally, we must never
outgrow dependence on God. The reason numerous people are going to
hell is because they refuse to depend on Jesus Christ for salvation and
try to earn it by their own merit. Therefore,It is okay to depend on
others when we need to.

While dependence, especially for daily life survival and sustenance,
seems to come to humans by default, independence has to be learned.

                                                              40
                                     THE WISDOM OF INDEPENDENCE

As it relates to taking responsibility for one’s own life outcomes,
dependence seems okay at certain stages, but at some point it begins to
look ugly.

Moses prayed for Judah, “Hear, Lord, the voice of Judah, and bring him
to his people; let his hands be sufficient for him, and may You be a help
against his enemies.” (Deut. 33:7). The prayer for one’s hand to be
sufficient for him/her is very important. It means that one has means to
meet personal needs and rise up to one’s life responsibilities without
dependence on another for survival or sustenance. It is wisdom to lean
dependently on God and God-given people at some points in life but it
is necessary wisdom to pursue independence in life.

In basic examples, a person who cannot afford a home of his own and is
putting up with someone is not yet independent; a person who needs
other people or even the government to support before they can feed is
not independent. It is important to take up responsibility and pursue
independence and freedom because our highest potential, most times,
manifests when we learn to stand without human crutches.

Independence is a requirement for good leadership. Leadership involves
learning to be independent of the followers’ resources as far as meeting
your needs is concerned. In other words, a leader must develop faith
and capacity to have his/her needs met without dependence on the
follower. A leader that is a burden on the followers is not a true leader.
The very spirit of leadership is the flow of honour from the led to the
leader. Dependence on the part of the leader destroys the fabric of that
honour.
This is the reason Paul said, ‘make it your ambition to lead a quiet life:
You should mind your own business and work with your hands, just as we
told you. so that your daily life may win the respect of outsiders and so

                                                              41
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

that you will not be dependent on anybody.’ (1 Thess. 4:11 -12 NIV) He
added in 2 Thess. 3:6, ‘Our orders—backed up by the Master, Jesus—are
to refuse to have anything to do with those among you who are lazy and
refuse to work the way we taught you. Don't permit them to freeload on
the rest. We showed you how to pull your weight when we were with you,
so get on with it. We didn't sit around on our hands expecting others to
take care of us. In fact, we worked our fingers to the bone, up half the
night moonlighting so you wouldn't be burdened with taking care of us.
And it wasn't because we didn't have a right to your support; we did. We
simply wanted to provide an example of diligence, hoping it would prove
contagious (The Message).

There are many forms of dependence but they start mostly with
financial or emotional dependence. Financial dependence is when you
do not have the means of resources to meet your own needs and always
have to fall back on someone else. This robs people of the freedom of
self-determination and decision. The highest gift God gave man is self-
will and lack of independence robs one of this. Thus, pursuing financial
independence will go a long way in positioning you to fulfil your
destiny. Financial independence is the state of having systems in place
that generate income whether you are actively involved or not, so that
your time is free to do other things for the rest of your life. It comes as a
result of having consistent residual and passive income that is above
your total expenditure, whose cash flow continues for the rest of your
life whether you continue to work or not. It is also in the spirit of
independence that one must seek not to be totally dependent on a job or
boss for a lifetime.

Emotional dependence is the inability to survive and thrive without the
involvement of a particular person, system or thing in your life.

                                                              42
                                     THE WISDOM OF INDEPENDENCE

It is a needy and uncontrollable state of attachment to a person or thing
for your sense of wholeness. Emotional and spiritual dependence is
more sinister than financial dependence many times. It is one reason
people stay in abusive relationships, it is at the base of wrong
associations and substance addictions. The only person we are called to
be totally emotionally and spiritually dependent on is God, not a
parent, friend, spouse, a man/woman of God or even a spouse.
Even in spousal relationships, emotional and spiritual dependence is
God’s will. God has not called you to be emotionally or spiritually
dependent on your partner, that space is His alone in your life.

What God wants is interdependence. Interdependence is the state of
being emotionally, spiritually and financially stable, but willingly
surrendering one’s independence to be dependent on another in some
areas while the other person is equally dependent on one in some areas
too. This births interdependence for mutual support of each other.

Independence is not the goal of life; interdependence is. However, a
dependent person cannot get into a phase of interdependence with
others. There is a level of independence and stability that is requisite
before one can be in a relationship where you receive and provide
reciprocal value.
All healthy and balanced relationships are based on interdependence.
Interdependence is hinged on development of self‐ value first. So every
man started dependent; we were dependent on parents, relatives and
people around. He/she must then deliberately pursue independence and
when he gets it, he realises that he needs people but he also has value in
himself to realise that they need him as well. Ultimately, he lays down
this independence willingly to give, receive and live interdependently on
others. Thus, there is also the wisdom of interdependence.

