                                 CHAPTER 11

              THE WISDOM OF CHANGE

Change is often desired and often feared. This is because change is
accompanied by risk, inconvenience and sometimes, pain. Many people
are very reluctant to change, and only do so when the pain of remaining
the same exceeds the pain of change. It takes the bold, the self-driven,
the ambitious and the confident one to initiate personal and corporate
change. Wisdom many times reveals itself in the ability to know what,
when, how and where to effect change. This is the reason it is often said
that ‘the ability to change is a measure of intelligence’.
One great mistake people often make is wishing for change without
changing anything. The truth is that nothing changes until things are
changed. Some people even harbour the thought that a change of year
(that wonderful ‘happy new year’ feeling) will automatically lead to a
change of life. Nothing can be further from the truth. Wisdom is
knowing what to change in order to change your situation.

Numbers 23: 19 says, God is not a man, so he does not lie. He is not
human, so he does not change his mind . . . . Active proponents of this
scripture have rightfully emphasised the point that it is unlike God to
change. Many have missed the salient point that this scripture hereby
acknowledges, that it is absolutely normal for man to change. In fact,
never changing would be abnormal for a man, because then, he would
be laying claim to being God. I guess you are not GOD, therefore, you
need to be open to change.

                                                              49
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

God says, I am the Lord, and I do not change . . . A quality of God is
that He does not change. The flip side of this statement is that the
quality of man is change. The reason God does not change is not
because He detests change, but because He does not need to. God has
factored all things from eternity past, present and future into view
before He acts, speaks or decides, so, He will never need to change who
He is, what He did or what He said.

Without change, there is no difference between yesterday and today.
Without change, there won’t be a difference between today and
tomorrow. The most important factor in life, growth and success is not
the passage of time, but the effecting of positive change. Every progress
in life will be as a result of making intentional decisions towards
positive change.
This does not mean we should change everything and at every time But
as said, ‘the main dangers in this life are the people who want to change
everything—or nothing. Thus, the most dangerous and most
endangered people are those who want to change everything and those
who want nothing to change.

