                                 CHAPTER 12

                THE WISDOM OF WORK

The first revelation of God in scripture is that He is a God that works.
The very first verse in scripture defines God as Creator. Creation of
anything is a tasking work, both mentally and physically. In fact, Gen
2:2 says by the seventh day God had finished the work he had been
doing; so on the seventh day he rested from all his work. God is working,
therefore, man created in His image and likeness must be working.

Man was created to work. The Bible says “Now the Lord God had
planted a garden in the east, in Eden; and there he put the man he had
formed. The Lord God made all kinds of trees grow out of the ground -
trees that were pleasing to the eyes and good for food.….the Lord God
took the man and put him in the Garden of Eden to work it and take care
of it. Ans the Lord commanded the man, You are free to eat from any tree
in the garden; but you must not eat from the tree of the knowledge of good
and evil, for when you eat from it, you will certainly die.’’ (Gen2: 8, 9,15-
17). The first thing God gave man after He created Him was work. It is
amazing that God created all that man needed for food in the garden,
but still gave him work nonetheless. This shows that the purpose of
work is not to have food to eat but to fulfil the divine mandate of
productivity. Earning money, food, clothing and shelter are side
benefits of work. Work in itself has intrinsic value, benefits and worth.
The average person, if freely given all that is needed for survival may see
no reason to exert himself in productive labour. A wise person, when
given all needed for sustenance,

                                                              52
                                             THE WISDOM OF WORK

sees that as an opportunity to work at their life vision and assignment
and not for survival.

Wise people are industrious and productive. Diligent work is the nature
of God and it is the culture of kingdom citizen. Diligence at work is
wisdom and laziness is foolishness. Whether the work is your personal
vision or you are employed in another person’s vision, how dilligent you
are at work is a measure of your character. In John 5:17, Jesus says, "
My Father never stops working, so why should I? " This shows that God
the Father is always working and Jesus the Son is working. 1
Corinthians 12:11 also says, But one and the same Spirit works all these
things . . . .’’ Thus, the Holy Spirit is also working. Now, if the Father,
Son and the Holy Spirit are working. Then how do you explain a
believer who is not working. There must be something you can do, you
had better get to diligent work!

While work was not originally created by God for earning a living but
for fulfilling life purpose, working to earn in today’s world is legitimate
wisdom. So, getting a job so that you can earn a living is the starting
point of progress for a person financially stranded. Contrary to the
popular motivational speakers’ cliches, ‘don’t work for money, let
money work for you!’ Working for money is prestigious and
honourable. Especially when it is accompanied with the financial
intelligence to make the money earned later work for you and build
wealth. Employment work (a job) is most of the time, a good starting
place for those who have no personal or inherited fortune to start with
before they proceed to intrapreneurial work and subsequently to
entrepreneurial work. Wealth and riches is linked to work. Do not be
ashamed of working no matter how menial or unprestigious the job
seems. Start from there, but have a resolute vision to build something

                                                              53
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

greater for yourself. Living without working is wasting life.

There are different levels of work. There is physical work,
mental/intellectual work and spiritual work. Physical exertion is
necessary for productivity. Sedentariness due to laziness causes diseases,
failure and poverty. Prov. 6: 6 instructs ‘‘take a lesson from the ants, you
lazybones. Learn from their ways and become wise! Though they have no
prince or governor or ruler to make them work, they labor hard all
summer, gathering food for the winter. But you, lazybones, how long will
you sleep? When will you wake up? A little extra sleep, a little more
slumber, a little folding of the hands to rest— then poverty will pounce on
you like a bandit; scarcity will attack you like an armed robber’’.
Intellectual work is tasking your mind to create solutions. As great as
physical diligence is, intellectual diligence is even more rewarding.
Those who task their minds will employ those who only task their
bodies. Reading, intellectual development, learning skills, taking
courses, thinking and writing are all work. I often ask students, ‘how is
work?’ and some reply, ‘I am not working, I am a student?’ I did not
know students only play. Until you approach schooling as work, you
can’t make something great of your academics. Also, in addition to
academics, work to earn, make money and develop yourself as a
student.
The third level of work is spiritual work. Spiritual work controls and
determines the outcome of all other levels of work. When one labours
physically and intellectually but is lazy spiritually, such a person is
exposed to the risk of fruitless labour. Make sure all your physical and
mental exertions are backed up with adequate spiritual efforts, else one
stands the chance of being a victim despite doing all things right in the
natural. Spiritual work includes prayers, fasting, giving and sacrifices,
studying, meditation and confessing God’s word. In John 6:28-29, some

                                                              54
                                             THE WISDOM OF WORK

people asked Jesus, "What must we do to do the works God requires?"
