                                                              55
                                 CHAPTER 13

              THE WISDOM OF IMPACT

One of the wisest decisions in life is the decision to live for impact.
There is a difference between accomplishment and impact.
Accomplishments are the additions you make for yourself. Impact is the
addition you make to others. An accomplished person may not be
impactful, but it is possible to be both accomplished and impactful. If
you ever have to choose between being accomplished and being
impactful, choose both!

Positive impact is one's strength to cause positive effect or change in the
lives of others. Impact is one's ability to modify people's situation,
lifestyle and experience through concentrated actions, relationships and
conversations with them. The end-point of impact is to inspire change
from the present to a more desirable future for people. It involves giving
your time, resources, ability, money and sometimes, your entire self and
life so that others can have a better life.

Genuine impact stems from selfless service rendered for the betterment
of others. It is absolutely correct to measure people’s greatness by the
weight of their positive impact on others and not merely the abundance
of their possessions and accomplishments. God’s purpose for your life is
impact. Your life purpose is to glorify God and impact humanity
through fulfilling your God-given assignment. So, you are created by
God to impact your generation in your identified sphere(s) of influence
through your life assignment.

                                                              56
                                            THE WISDOM OF IMPACT

Jesus declares in John 12:8 "I am the light of the world: he that follows
me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life." Jesus
walked the earth to bring light to those who lived in darkness. He came
to the world to release man held in bondage and to give light to the
darkened soul of man - that is impact! He said "As long as I am in the
world, I am the light of the world." (John 9: 5). This means that His
baton of Kingdom impact is automatically transferred to all His
followers whenever He leaves the earth. Thus, as Christians, we are
mandated for a life of impact by our Lord, Matt 5: 14 - 16, "You are the
light of the world—like a city on a hilltop that cannot be hidden. No one
lights a lamp and then puts it under a basket. Instead, a lamp is placed on
a stand, where it gives light to everyone in the house. 16 In the same way,
let your good deeds shine out for all to see, so that everyone will praise
your heavenly Father. One is living when people’s lives and wellbeing are
being enhanced because one is alive. Otherwise, one is just existing.
The primal impact every believer is to make is to impact the people of
the world with the “Light of the Gospel of Christ”. Proverbs 11:30 says
"The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life; and he that winneth souls is
wise." We have been made righteous in Christ and we are only meant to
produce fruits of life in those around us. The greatest of this life-giving
fruit is soul winning. Whilst it is vital to be helpful to humanity and be
benevolent to people generally, the greatest impact a Christian can
