                                                              92
                                 CHAPTER 23

          THE WISDOM OF ASSOCIATION

The relationships around you are an adequate measure and an accurate
prediction of the level of your wisdom and the quality of your persona.
People who have a good number of high quality persons as the
reciprocal relationships in their immediate networks are those who have
capacity and value themselves. If you want to have a fair guess at the
quality of character, capacity, competence and value, check the
reciprocal relationships in your life. A reciprocal relationship is one in
which the person is interested in you and you are interested in them. A
reciprocal relationship is not parasitic and is not one in which you are
clinging to or pursuing someone who only does not know how to do
away with you. A reciprocal relationship is a symbiotic relationship and
there is mutual derivation of value and reciprocal respect.

Great people do not spend time with nonentities. Thus, if you are in a
network of 10 mediocre persons, you are the eleventh, no rocket science
about that. One of the surest ways to change your life is to change your
associations. Proverbs 13:20 says, He that walks with wise men shall be
wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed. The person who
associates with the great stands a great chance to be great.

You must be deliberate in choosing the relationships in your life. There
should be an invisible circle around your space with an invisible door
that determines who you let in and who you do not.

                                                              93
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

While we are to be loving and friendly to everyone, know today that
you cannot give everyone access to yourself. The people you listen to
and relate with are the greatest determinant of who you are becoming in
life. This includes the church you attend, the school you go to, the
colleagues you work with, the books you read, the movies you watch,
the people you follow on social media. The law of association is all
encompassing.

Jesus wanted to choose the twelve people that would be closest to Him
in His earthly walk and spent an entire night praying. This shows us
that we must be prayerful and spiritually sensitive in deciding who we
allow to cross from one level of relationship to another with us. There
are different levels of relationships in a person's life. There are strangers,
acquaintances, friends and family, inner circles and confidants. Do not
give people a place they do not belong with you. The rules of relating
with people at these levels are different. You have to pray before
allowing people into certain levels of your life space.

The difference between you today and tomorrow is your association.
This is the reason you need to be deliberate in going after advantageous
relationships. Relationships with great people are an asset. You need
godly, successful and rich people in your life. Pray for God to send such
people to your life. Develop yourself so that you will be valuable
enough to have a reciprocal relationship with such people. Remember;
help the poor, love them sincerely and don’t despise them but partner
with the rich. Partnering and walking with the poor is dangerous
foolishness.

It is utmost foolishness to give everybody equal access to yourself. The
higher you go or you are working to go in life, the more streamlined the

