                                                              96
                                 CHAPTER 24

           THE WISDOM OF PARENTING

There is a huge difference between being a parent and progenitor. This
is because it is not biological procreation that confers parenthood. It is
a mindset and practice of nurturing. The word ‘Father’ in the Greek is
the word ‘Pater’. It means source, nurturer, origin and principal/leader.
The purpose of fatherhood is foremost to transfer nature and DNA to
an offspring and thereafter nurture it to its full potential. Paternity is
the ability to impart a nature on another and nurture that nature till full
stature.

Nature and stature, nurtured by a parent, is not limited to the physical,
it includes the spiritual, intellectual, academic, financial and other vital
areas of life. Thus, the offspring of a billionaire is automatically a rich
child and the offspring of an academician stands every chance of being
academically advantaged. Thus, a major role of parenthood is to
transfer the possibility and potentials to another and thereafter raise
that person till they become and attain that potential. Exceptional
parents nurture offspring who surpass them in nature. In other words, a
good parent raises children that are better and greater than them in
their area of advantage. This shows that how well you perform as a
parent in an area of life is measured eventually by your children’s
attainment not merely yours. However, your children’s attainment will
eventually be determined - strengthened or weakened by your
development in that area of life.

                                                              97
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

Parenthood is a huge demand and responsibility. A parent is pushing
and gunning for more in life because they realise that what they become
will be their children’s life advantage or otherwise. The foremost
wisdom of parenthood is preparation in capacity building - spiritually,
mentally, academically, financially and emotionally.

Gen 4:20-21 talks about Jabal who was the father of such as dwell in
tents, and of such as have cattle. And his brother, Jubal who was the
father of all such as handle the harp and organ. Jabal was the first person
to domesticate human living and animal rearing. Before him, all
humans were wanderers, hunters and food-gatherers, with a nomadic
lifestyle. He parented a generation of people who lived an established
home life. His brother, Jubal, was the first musician in human history
and parented a generation of musician. The normal rule of life is that
your children stand every chance of becoming what you are. There are
exceptions to this rule but we don’t build principles on exceptions, we
build on the rule. This profound wisdom is what singles need so as to be
conscious that when they are choosing a spouse, they are actually
choosing a nature, potential and a future for their children. In choosing
a marital partner, don't just be focused on choosing a spouse for
yourself, consider strongly the fact that you are choosing a parent for
your children as well. The traits and lifestyle you would want to see in
your children is what you look for in a spouse.

Many people are not building the capacity to be parents. unmarried,
married or single parents, the growth and development in parenthood
capacity must still continue. The truth is that God, in His
predestination, many times allocates children to selected parents based
on the destiny He has chosen for such unique children by His election of
grace.

