                                 CHAPTER 26

           THE WISDOM OF UTTERANCE

It is wisdom to keep quiet when you should keep quiet and it is wisdom
to speak when you should speak. Knowing the what, when and how of
making utterance correctly is one of the highest indices of wisdom. You
must make it an ambition to always know what to say and the right
time to say it. People have gotten into trouble by what they said even
more than by what they did. Utterance, many times, implicates people
more than actions.

Words are actually meant to be for communication and also to
disseminate information, but it is not everything that is meant to be
verbalised. Silence, gesture, countenance, disposition are all forms of
communication. So wisdom of utterance is knowing what type of
utterance is best at a particular time.

For an intention to be verbalized, utterances have to be made. So
verbalisation is crucial in communication. Thus, maximise your right
and freedom to speak, but understand that one can either speak his way
to life or speak his way to death. Prov. 18: 21 says, Death and Life are in
the power of the tongue, and those who love it will eat its fruit. The truth
is that people speak, but only few speak as guided by the wisdom of
utterance. The wisdom of utterance is the wisdom to know what to say,
when to speak, how to present it, to whom to speak to/with and if need
be, when to keep silent.

                                                             106
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

It is also important to know that Satan, demons and wicked people do
not know so much about you; they mostly depend on your utterance to
deduce facts about you. So, make it your commitment to keep them
clueless about your destiny and situations by relying completely on the
Holy Spirit to be the gatekeeper of your mouth, and let the Word of
God be your default utterance at the face of occurrences.

This Wisdom of utterance is the ability to speak the right words at the
right time, and present your utterances in the right manner. Proverbs
16:23 (AMP) says, the mind of the wise instructs his mouth, and adds
learning and persuasiveness to his lips. This shows that a wise person
does not just speak because he feels like speaking or he is asked to, he
speaks only as instructed by spiritual, emotional and mental
intelligence. Always intelligently weigh the consequences of your
utterances before you make them. A wise person knows the
consequence of every utterance and only speaks for intended
consequence.

Another key component of the Wisdom of Utterance is speaking boldly
when you need to. Declaring spiritual words over physical realities is
spiritual wisdom. You should not keep your mouth closed in spiritual
warfare. Putting the Word of God on your lips and declaring it boldly
in the face of contrary is wisdom. If Satan, situations or the enemy says
anything contrary to you, it is not wisdom to keep quiet. Decree back
what you want to see, that daring utterance is wisdom. In spiritual
warfare, utterance is a necessity. Discretion in speech is needed before
men but in the realms of the spirit, the wisdom of utterance is
demonstrated by bold speaking and daring declarations. Ultimately, the
utterance is only available through yielding to the Holy Spirit. The Holy
Spirit prompts you on when to speak and when to be quiet.

                                                             107
                                        THE WISDOM OF UTTERANCE

The Bible says in Proverbs 25:11 "The right word spoken at the right
time is as beautiful as gold apples in a silver bowl." This literally means,
words could be “mud” when spoken at the wrong time; but by rightness
of timing, it becomes gold. You must daily pray and yield to the Holy
