                THE WISDOM OF LOVE

Walking in wisdom is walking in love. Whenever one steps out of love,
one steps into errors. Whenever you are faced with alternatives and a
crisis of choices, it is helpful to always ask yourself, ‘what would love
do?’ You cannot be wrong when you choose the way of love.

“I can never be wrong when I choose the way of love”. I know a
thousand and one people that followed the way of love and went
wrong’, someone might be quick to ask. They would further furnish
examples of lovers that were cheated, broken, offended, taken for
granted, or even destroyed. They would challenge the statement that “
no one can be wrong following love”. Well, the truth is that the people
that went wrong following ‘love’ actually followed the ‘wrong kind of
love’. Certainly, you can never go wrong following the way of Real
Love.

It is common knowledge that the word ‘Love’ as used in English has
many equivalents in Greek, which is a language that offers a more
nuanced vocabulary for describing different facets of love. For instance,
in the Greek language, ‘Agape’ refers to unconditional or selfless
sacrifice for the wellbeing of another. ‘Philia’ represents affection,
fondness or friendly likeness for another. ‘Storge’ pertains to familiar or
cordial love and solidarity, while ‘Eros’ signifies romantic, passionate or
sexual attraction towards someone. All these words with widely
divergent and varied meanings and applications are all translated ‘Love’

                                                             110
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

in English. In fact, there are some other usages of the word love in
English that have a different Greek word other than the four described
above. The point is that the word ‘love’ in English has been so misused,
misunderstood, and bastardised that it seems to have lost its power due
to the fact that a lot of wrong labels have been placed on ‘love’. Love
can never go wrong or fail. Real love is Agape - the God-Kind of Love.
Many things mislabelled as ‘love’ have all gone wrong and have given
Love a bad name.

1 John 4:7-9 says, Beloved, let us love one another, for love is of God; and
everyone who loves is born of God and knows God. He who does not love
does not know God, for God is love. (NKJV). God is love! So, what God
would do in every situation is what love would do. Do you now see that
the way of love is the way of wisdom? When you are faced with a
situation and you don’t know how to react or what step to take, ask
yourself; ‘what would God do if He was in my shoes? How would Jesus
react if He was here? What God would have done is the way of love -
Choose that way and you would have acted wisely.

In Mark 12:28-31, One of the teachers of religious law was standing . . .
so he asked, "Of all the commandments, which is the most important?"
Jesus replied, "The most important commandment is this: 'Listen, O
Israel! The LORD our God is the one and only LORD. And you must
LOVE the LORD your God with all your heart, all your soul, all your
mind, and all your strength.' The second is equally important: 'LOVE
your neighbor as yourself.' No other commandment is greater than these."
Love is the greatest instruction, so Love is the greatest wisdom.

According to Rom 13:9-10, For the commandments, "Do not commit
adultery, do not murder, do not steal, do not covet,"

                                                             111
                                              THE WISDOM OF LOVE

(and if there is any other commandment) are summed up in this, "Love
