                                 CHAPTER 28

           THE WISDOM OF GRATITUDE

There are some practices that are doses to live a happy and healthy life.
These habits power up and secure a life of bliss, strength and hope. One
of such practice is living a lifestyle of immense gratitude for every gift of
life. Gratitude is an act that begins from a heart that recognizes a
blessing, and then responds to that blessing by acknowledgement and
appreciation. Grateful people are thoughtful people, who will look for a
reason to give thanks, even in a seeming unpleasant situation, rather
than being encumbered with worries and complaints. In positive
psychology research, gratitude is strongly and consistently associated
with greater happiness. Gratitude helps people feel more positive
emotions, relish good experiences, improve their health, deal with
adversity, and build strong relationships. Grateful people live under an
atmosphere of hope, which make them immune to any dart of sorrow
and grief life throws at them. A grateful person is not just grateful
because every line is falling in right places; but even when things seem
not to go as planned, they have a beautiful sigh of "it is well." to
express. Gratitude stems from a depth of understanding that is rooted
in the knowledge of God's goodness.

A simple utterance of "thank you" from a sincere heart can act as a
catalyst to speed up a function and usher one into great success.
Gratitude should be a language of communication between people in
their various homes, workplaces and schools.

                                                             115
                                        THE WISDOM OF GRATITUDE

In an environment where gratitude is relatively expressed; relationships
are strengthened, there is fostering of goodwill, and promotion of
positive emotions. Gratitude is a strong index to measure one's spiritual,
mental, emotional and social health. In an atmosphere of expressive
gratitude, there is multiplication and preservation. Thanksgiving secures
the received blessing and procures the favour to receiving more
blessings.

God is good and rich unto all, but He is unapologetically gracious to
people who have mastered the art of thanking Him for every little thing
in their lives. In the Bible, there are many cases of people whose lifestyle
of gratitude to God made them highly preferred above their peers,
prolonged their lives, multiplied their resources, fortified their camps
and engendered God's power to turn hopeless situation around. One of
such occurrences is seen in the book of 2Chronicles 20: 1-25 "(vs. 21:)
And when he had consulted with the people, he appointed singers unto the
Lord, and that should praise the beauty of holiness, as they went out
before the army, and to say, Praise the Lord; for his mercy endureth for
ever." In a situation that seems defeat and destruction is imminent, the
wisdom of gratitude teaches to look away from the tempestuous wind of
life and set one's gaze on Jesus only, giving thanks and reassuring
oneself of His steadfast love and unfailing mercy.

Apostle Paul in the New Testament exhorts in 1Thess. 5:16-18 "Rejoice
always, pray continually, give thanks in all circumstances; for this is God’s
