setting OTHERS into purpose and fulfilment. "And in the morning,
rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a
solitary place, and there prayed." (Mk. 1:35) Jesus devoted an ample
part of his time to prayers, setting himself apart in solitude to build up
himself, and to receive divine revelations and instructions from God, on
what to do per time and season. So, prayer will first of all build you up,
and then equip and empower you to build your life, destiny and vision.
Men who are built up by prayer become strong and able men, who live
above every limitation, brought down every stronghold of darkness and
wrought great exploits as victors and conquerors. Men who pray,
consistently evolve into the better version of themselves; for every
second spent in prayer is an investment unto betterment, increase and
expansion. The Bible clearly captured it in Jude 1:26 (Amp), "But you,
beloved, build yourselves up [founded] on your most holy faith [make
progress, rise like an edifice higher and higher], praying in the Holy
Spirit;" Prayer is a builder. As one prays in the building language of the
Spirit; there is constantly an upgrade. A small and fearful person can
pray up himself into a strong giant, to do valiantly, and function in
various dimensions of graces, as unlocked by prayers.

Then, what responsibility of destiny has God committed into your

                                                             120
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

hands? What assignment has God given to you? What vision has God
revealed in your heart? What career has God given you as an ambition?
What business idea has God ideated in your mind? What ministry has
God ordained you for? PRAY! It is foolish to receive the blueprint of
one's destiny from God and then start running with it by human
philosophies and principles. The God who gave the architectural plan is
also interested in the building process. And this is by prayer. "O Lord, I
know that the way of man is not in himself: it is not in man that walketh to
direct his steps." (Jer. 10:23) When God shows the way, He is keenly
interested in leading the way, and guiding one's feet step by step. A wise
man understands that "there is a way that seemeth right unto a man, but
the end thereof are the ways of death. (Prov. 16:25) So, he depends on
God completely to order his steps and to dictate his moves. And this is
as he prays. Prayer is an enforcer by which one enforces the promises of
God over one's life into reality. Prayer is also a means by which one
tenders one's petitions before God, supplicating for His provisions in
alignment with His Will for one's life.

And lastly, prayer sets up others into the discoveries of their purpose in
God, and preserves them unto fulfilment. A person can pray another
into the Will of God for their lives, insisting on the salvation of their
souls and that they should respond to their high callings in God. This
prayer is called the prayer of intercession; standing in gap for others to
set them up for a life of godliness and glory. There is a portion in the
scriptures that portrays intercession as an act of God's Love and mercy
to restore men unto himself, by raising up other men to stand in gap for
them. "I have set watchmen upon thy walls, O Jerusalem, which shall
never hold their peace day nor night: ye that make mention of the Lord,
keep not silence. And give him no rest, till he establish, and till he make
Jerusalem a praise in the earth." (Isa. 62:6-7)

                                                             121
                                           THE WISDOM OF PRAYER

As believers, prayer is not a choice, it is not an option. Prayer should be
our natural lifestyle. Jesus did not say "if" you pray as a function of
your choice, but "when" you pray, as an expected way of living that one
need not to be coerced or begged into. Prayer is man's will of
acknowledging God as the planner, builder and rewarder of his destiny.

                                                             122
                                 CHAPTER 30

    THE WISDOM OF PROPHETIC BLESSINGS

It is great wisdom to position one’s life for an operation under open
heavens. ‘Open Heavens’ is a term generally used to describe a
favourable spiritual climate over a person’s life and destiny that makes
the spiritual realm work in the person’s advantage thereby producing
desirable physical outcomes.

The truth is that, having engaged all the wisdom keys outlined in this
book, it is important to note that the spiritual climate over a person’s
life and destiny is the ultimate determinant of their life results. The
spiritual realm utterly controls the physical, and having done all that
needs to be done in the natural, one must know how to engage available
spiritual advantage.

At times, it is not merely the absence of doing the right things in the
natural - all the things which have been largely portrayed in this book -
that is responsible for the presence of certain life limitations. Many
times, it is because there is something in the spiritual realm that needs to
be engaged. The story of Job is a classic example of the hold the
spiritual has over the physical. Job was successful, having all going well
at a moment and the next moment, he was down to ashes. All this did
not happen because he did anything differently in the natural realm but
because a negotiation happened concerning him in the spiritual which
he was even oblivion to.

                                                             123
                                 THE WISDOM OF PROPHETIC PRAYERS

The spiritual legislates over the natural at any time, on any day. Like
Job, there are many people whose physical state is as a result of a
spiritual transaction which they may not even be party in its
negotiation. Spiritual intelligence and wisdom is knowing what to do to
trigger the spiritual realm to work in one’s advantage.

One among the key principles for engaging spiritual advantage is to
have a voice that supplies prophetic cover and advantage to one’s
destiny. This means, it is wise to have a grace and voice you are
connected and submitted to for prophetic blessings. It is important to
have someone that is higher than you in the spirit that releases blessings
over you and the work of your hand. You need to recognize the fathers,
mothers, and spiritual authorities that God has set over you and
position yourself for a continual flow of words of blessings in your
direction from them. A word of wisdom, however, is to note that you
should be led by God to the spiritual authority to submit your life
under. It is not something to be window-shopped for or to be chosen
based on likeness for a famous prophetic figure you seemingly admire.
The prophet over your life that will have the right heart for you and the
right words for your destiny in his/her mouth is usually a gift to be
allocated by God to each individual.

In the Book of Ezra, the Jews were building the Temple, led by
Zerubbabel the Governor of the land and Joshua the High Priest but
Bible recounts that they succeeded because as some people were
working physically, there were prophetic voices supplying spiritual
backup to them. This is shown in Ezra 6: 14, ‘and the elders of the Jews
builded, and they prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the
prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. And they builded, and finished it,
according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the

                                                             124
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

commandment of Cyrus, and Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia’
Generally, people prosper because there is a voice speaking in the realm
of the spirit speaking on their behalf. The people of the world, the
unbelievers and the practitioners of darkness understand this fact very
well and they will seldom do anything until they have leveraged on
spiritual advantage from their ‘prophets of the realm of darkness.’ It is
children of God’s kingdom that has been poisoned by the spirit of
deception to despise their own prophets and pastors. No matter how
great or kingly you are in the natural, your success is largely dependent
on submission to a spiritual leader for continuous supply of spiritual
grace, blessing and advantage. This is deep wisdom.

In the Old Testament, three categories of people were anointed over the
nation of Israel: the king, the priests and the prophet. The king and
priest provide executive, judicial and legislative leadership while the
prophet provided spiritual leadership. The nation experienced blessings
when the king submitted to the spiritual fatherhood and authority of a
genuine prophet of God. The country experienced problems when the
king rebelled against the instructions and spiritual cover of the prophet.
The spiritual is superior to the natural. It does not matter your position
in the natural, there must be a fountain of spiritual blessings that speaks
over your life.

At certain points in the history of Israel, Samuel was Prophet over the
nation. He released prophetic blessings over Saul as king and as long as
the king submitted to his fatherhood and blessings, he reigned in
prosperity. After Saul rebelled against his prophetic cover, God led
Samuel to place the prophetic blessing on David. David lived his entire
life under the prophetic blessing and fatherly covering. At a point when
Saul was after his life, he ran to meet his spiritual father in Ramah.

                                                             125
                                 THE WISDOM OF PROPHETIC PRAYERS

According to 1 Sam 19:18-24, so David escaped and went to Ramah to
see Samuel, and he told him all that Saul had done to him. Then Samuel
took David with him to live at Naioth. When the report reached Saul that
David was at Naioth in Ramah, he sent troops to capture him. But when
they arrived and saw Samuel leading a group of prophets who were
prophesying, the Spirit of God came upon Saul's men, and they also began
to prophesy. When Saul heard what had happened, he sent other troops,
but they, too, prophesied! The same thing happened a third time. Finally,
Saul himself went to Ramah and arrived at the great well in Secu. "Where
are Samuel and David?" he demanded. "They are at Naioth in Ramah,"
someone told him. But on the way to Naioth in Ramah the Spirit of God
came even upon Saul, and he, too, began to prophesy all the way to
Naioth! He tore off his clothes and lay naked on the ground all day and all
night, prophesying in the presence of Samuel. The people who were
watching exclaimed, "What? Is even Saul a prophet?"

David ran under Samuel’s prophetic cover when the battle became a life
and death matter. The battle that seemed so great for David to fight
proved to be too small for Samuel who did not even lift a finger but all
the armies of Saul and eventually Saul himself were disgraced and fell
under the power of God, the moment they came around the
circumference of the spiritual atmosphere of Samuel where David hid.
The issues that look like a big problem in your life may just need a
simple word of prayer from a spiritual authority. However, the question
is do you have one over your life that you are actively connected to?

When Samuel died, the Bible records King David’s submission to the
prophetic authority and cover of Prophet Nathan who was more of an
age contemporary to King David (2 Sam. 7: 4, 2 Sam 12: 1). The truth is
that prophetic cover is not by age, it is by grace.

                                                             126
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

You may be older or age-mate with someone, but if they rank higher
than you in the spirit and God wants you to submit to them for a flow
of prophetic blessings, please condescend and don’t relate to your
prophet as an equal.

Your destiny will always need prophetic help, so have a spiritual
covering that can shield you in and out of seasons. Spiritual leaders are
called fathers in the Old Testament and elders in the New. They are
positioned to bring an advantage to your life and help you go farther in
life. They are to provide a spiritual shield for you especially in tough
seasons of life. The battle you have been fighting for long can be easily
settled by prophetic intervention. This strategy is God’s wisdom to keep
His people humble and procure honour for His servants. Prophetic
blessing can also be released by biological parents in addition to pastors
and spiritual leaders. It is the principle of submission to authority for a
flow of blessing. The blessing is stronger than curses. The reason curses
have seemed strong is that we have not being well taught the principle
of the blessing - the blessing from submission to someone you see as
greater than you. Heb 7:7 says, ‘now beyond all contradiction the lesser is
blessed by the greater’.

While it is true that every child of God is blessed with every spiritual
blessings in the heavenly realms (Eph. 1: 3) and has direct access to the
blessing of Abraham through Jesus Christ (Gal 3: 14), God’s
systematized protocol of the blessing is that it is released upon a man
and transferred from that man to every other person. This is the reason
even Abraham the father of faith needed to be blessed by Melchizedek
(Gen 14: 18 - 24). Jesus blessed the bread and gave it to the apostles to
transfer to the Church (John 6: 11, Mark 14: 22- 24). This shows that
there was no way to access the blessing of Jesus Christ except one

                                                             127
                                 THE WISDOM OF PROPHETIC PRAYERS

 received it through his disciples then. The apostles have passed the
message and the blessing over to many people and there are billions of
people that have received the salvation and other blessings in Christ.
However, the principle still remains the same - the only way to receive
the blessing of God is through a man He has committed it to. This is the
wisdom of God to humble all men as they cannot access Him
completely independent of other people. The great disdain and
dishonour that Satan has planted in the heart of people for Christian
leaders, pastors and prophets by always propagating negative things
about them is his strategy to attach this power of prophetic cover and
blessings from them. This is because the blessing cannot flow to one
from a carrier that one does not honour. Sadly, many Christians in
ignorance are partners and propagators of Satan’s work of attacking
men of God. Please, desist from that foolishness, your prophetic
advantage is in the mouth of a man of God.

                                                             128
                                 CHAPTER 31

   CONCLUSION - THE WISDOM OF ETERNITY

Classically, there are three orders of event in a man's life: his birth, his
death and the life he lived in between; which then decides the life he
would live after death. All through different ages and dispensations,
ample and apt exegesis has been done on time and living in time. There
are beautiful pieces of literature crafted by philosophers and theorists in
a bid to define and give meaning to the verity of time and the reality of
living. However, there hasn't been clarity and actual understanding of
the essence of the life lived in time and of how it affects the life lived
after time. And is it even true that there is some life after death? If there
is, where is that location? How do we go there? What do we do there?
What's it all about? These and many more are the myriad of questions
asked by the inquisitive minds of men, but only project further
confusions, because both the "what and how" of it is purely spiritual,
and can be conceived and understood only by a spiritual mind. These
vagueness and confusion is what the wisdom of eternity will by the
Spirit, bring to light.

The first place where the word "eternity" was mentioned In the Bible
(KJV) is in Isaiah 57:15a "For thus saith the high and lofty One that
inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy
place" Herein, we understand that God lives and inhabits himself in
eternity. What then is eternity? Eternity is a spiritual reality of a realm
and existence that is beyond time.

                                                             129
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

This is to say that eternity is an infinite space that exists outside the
circumference of time. It is a reality that cannot be measured by and in
time. In comparison, time is a measurable and finite existence that is
marked within the infinite and immeasurable existence called eternity.
So, we can rightly deduce that man is a being set out of eternity to live
in time for a definite period, and then having lived in time should exit
out of time to continue into eternity. To come into time, is by being
born to live for a while in time, and then to exit out of time through an
event called death. So, since man is a being set out of eternity by God to
live in time, then there will surely be a continuation of man's existence
after his life in time, and that; is his return to God in eternity. This
therefore justifies the reality of life after death.

The wisdom of eternity then teaches us to know that there is a direct
implication of the life lived by man in time on the life man will live after
time. A man's life should not just be lived as he wills nor as he pleases,
but according to the will and for the pleasure of He who set him in time.
This then explains the concept of purpose; that man does not just exist
in time only to die after some while, but that man should live only to
fulfil the purpose of why he exists in time.

God set man in time that he may carry out an assignment, fulfil a
mission and then return to God to be rewarded for his work on earth.
This means that man's life in time should be defined by his God-given
and life assignment. And This assignment is contained, discovered and
fulfilled. Because when man lost his compass and missed his way; God
reached out to man through Jesus as the only true way to bring man
back to himself. So, for man and his works to be accepted by God, he
has to

                                                             130
                                          THE WISDOM OF ETERNITY

be by his belief and confession of Jesus as Lord. Romans 10:9 "That if
thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine
heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved." So,
the only means by which man can fulfil his assignment and also by
which his eternal reward can be guaranted is by coming into Jesus as the
only true way to God. John 14:6 "Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the
truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me."

In the world today, there are many religions and sects who in one way
or the other believe that God is the object of their worship. They claim
to be servants and followers of God, but outside of the lordship of
Jesus. It's so unfortunate to see men labour religiously in good deeds
and morality, but only unto futility and vanity. Because there are not
many ways, but only one way to God, and that's through Jesus Christ.
Acts 4:12 "There is salvation in no one else, for there is no other name
under heaven given among men by which we must be saved."

Jesus during his ministry on earth, through stories and parables, gave
several accounts on the reality of life after death, and the aftermath of
the kind of life a person lived while on earth. Jesus always had a
common ending to those parables; as seen three times in the Gospel of
Matthew (8:12, 22:13, and 25:30) "But the children of the kingdom (not
of Christ) shall be cast out into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and
gnashing of teeth."
The wisest decision to make in life is the decision to secure one's
eternity, through Jesus Christ. One day, this earth will end; time will
cease to exist; nothing else will matter other than one's soul who will
give account of one's lifetime, and then procures God's judgment, either
to live with God forever or to be doomed unto eternal death and
damnation. Jesus once asked a powerful question which every living

                                                             131
                                                  31 WISDOM KEYS

soul must answer, Mark 8:36-37 "For what shall it profit a man, if he
shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? Or what shall a man give
in exchange for his soul?" The decision to secure one's eternity should
not be one to procrastinate, but to make just right NOW!!

To give your life to Jesus, say this prayer:

Lord Jesus, I believe in you as my Lord and Saviour. I ask that you come
into my life and save my soul. I receive the Life of God, and I live for God
alone. Henceforth, I am a child of God, and I reign over sin, sickness and
death. Thank you Jesus for saving me, Amen!

